## Shared decisions to preserve

- [ ] Keep the kernel domain-neutral: identities/occurrences/revisions; units/frames/clocks; supports/selections; typed values/evidence/unknowns; relations/constraints; operators/dependencies; purpose-specific representations; explicit runtime state. Workflows reuse these primitives rather than owning parallel model/save/query/undo systems.

- [ ] Keep ownership small: proposed pure `workspace_model` may depend on pure nucleus types; nucleus never imports it. Engine/store own authorized acceptance/persistence, native interface owns rendering/tools, map supplies geographic data, transport/Cell/Organ own scoped delivery, Protein retains semantic/source sessions, and specialist workers appear only when a stage needs them. Keep scientific kernels out of ordinary viewers.

- [ ] Treat Fiote as an Actor with the Agent role, acting within delegated scope through the same authorized queries, typed commands, validation, receipts, cancellation and undo as native controls. Use [stage 02's Agent contract](contracts/Durable-model-contracts.lingua#agent-actors-and-delegated-workspace-operations), [stage 04's bounded context](contracts/Selection-and-interface-contracts.lingua#structured-context-for-workspace-actors) and [stage 07's native authoring workflow](contracts/Native-authoring-and-behavior-contracts.lingua#native-scene-authoring-by-an-agent). Keep manual use complete when the provider is absent.

- [ ] Preserve one content/source identity across appropriate spatial, flat and HUD presentations, with view-local focus/tool state, independent anchors and aggregate demand budgets. Keep canonical placement and underlying Record/model state coherent; see [stage 03](contracts/Frames-and-views-contracts.lingua#content-and-presentation-identity). Use existing compositor/application adapters for supported external content.

- [ ] Derive linked work from explicit model selections, revisioned quantities and declared recipes. Update unaccepted derived drafts live while preserving manual overrides; reconcile accepted assignments, commitments and Transfers through their authoritative operations. [Stage 11](contracts/Assembly-and-character-contracts.lingua#revisioned-takeoff-for-linked-work) supplies inputs and [stage 13](contracts/Operational-workflow-contracts.lingua#live-derived-work-and-reconciliation) owns this workflow.

- [ ] Choose architecture for the concrete software capabilities in this sequence. Physical equipment integration, Dynamicware and Geist/world-model research add zero deliverables, dependencies or acceptance gates to Workspace. Electronic design and software simulation are explicit Workspace deliverables in stages 07/11a/15a/21. Reuse the needed model/view/input/observation/artifact boundaries; add no speculative adapter framework solely for future equipment. Real equipment validation remains in Ailuros; preserve existing calibration/output behavior where touched.

- [ ] Make scale scene-independent. The ball/Earth/solar route and independent invented scene are required examples, never fixed engine endpoints/hierarchy/zoom bands. Preserve local physical dimensions, exact authored distinctions, navigation up distinct from gravity, and sparse active cost independent of empty extent.

- [ ] Select Orbit/Fly/Walk explicitly; preserve supported pose/focus and horizon/street/interior use. Ground has no local relief and absent building/interior geometry stays absent unless supplied/authored. The globe remains curved; blank roots need no Earth. Map/overview proxies and street geometry identify the same user-authored place.

- [ ] Release unneeded RAM/GPU after bounded demand/fences; retain durable edits, bounded compressed disk cache and explicit offline packs. Fetch configured detail on demand online within persistent budgets; full workspace-offline starts no remote/source/heartbeat/reconnect request.

- [ ] Automatically apply ready applicable editor output to the captured selected local scope on exit; preserve pending/invalid/stale state and previous accepted output otherwise. Keep ordinary multi-copy editing simple, source lineage retained and deliberate shared-definition updates explicit. Exceptional unsupported continuation retains last usable output and pauses only affected evolution before a visible refresh/restart.

- [ ] Preserve scoped identity/rights: private invites plus optional explicit public visitors, identified authorized editors, optional nonphysical avatars/cursors and designated runtime authority. Entry cost/preflight is bounded and continuing limits are enforced. No invite lends another Organ's login, private source, execution, desktop/pixels/input or worker budget.

- [ ] Keep permitted cached viewing and drafts after host loss; revalidate/reconcile with the same authority and recorded request outcomes. Do not automatically replay mutations, elect a physics writer or donate participant compute. Distinguish accepted geometry, observations, operational facts and conditional results.

- [ ] Preserve direct empirical material choice without microscopic setup, independent specimen/laboratory roots and amount-versus-sample separation. Structural editing is stage 12; new property derivation and numerical physical prediction belong to the numerical packages with their own verified prerequisites. Stage 07 functional behavior is core and does not claim circuit/material physics. Atoms/proteins do not replicate by moles to simulate a bulk object.

- [ ] Model characters, animals, robots and mechanisms through the same articulated relations, reference configurations, pose coordinates, deformation bindings, attachments and motion/controller operators. Stage 05 supplies lightweight first/third-person navigation, stage 07 customizes supplied appearance, and [stage 11](contracts/Assembly-and-character-contracts.lingua#articulated-models-rigs-and-anatomy) delivers shared rig/pose/motion authoring and optional anatomical references. Preserve one model/command/save/query/undo path; do not make a humanoid skeleton or anatomy pack a kernel requirement.

- [ ] Control structural coverage, visible detail and calculated behavior independently. Detailed anatomical structures can unload after editing while a simpler surface, rig and support proxy retain authored behavior. Pose/animation authoring is core; additional force-driven joints, physical cloth/hair, active muscles, tissue mechanics and biomechanical predictions remain deferred. Fiote receives permitted named structures, captured poses and attributed annotations; clinical diagnosis is not a core capability or acceptance gate.

## Interchangeable behavior and electronics delivery

- [ ] **Owner refinement, 2026-11-01.** Deliver mixed authored, functional and physical behavior in the same workspace, with model choice per occurrence, assembly or explicitly selected domain. These planning changes authorize no implementation or completion claim. Preserve the earlier workflows and implementation review boundary.

- [ ] Keep five independent choices: **appearance**, **structural coverage/residency**, **behavior model per domain**, **numerical/temporal settings within that model**, and **active scope/resource policy**. There is no universal scalar fidelity ladder. A detailed PCB may use functional behavior; a box may run a circuit. Each domain supplies only its implemented models and transitions; an empty model slot is not a capability.

- [ ] Use one logical object with revisioned internal definitions, external ports and alternative behavior models. Start abstract and add internals later, or retain detailed internals and select an authored/imported/derived approximation. Each model declares supported inputs/outputs, state, purpose, conditions, provenance, dependencies and cost. Preserve requested observables and any established error bounds; a name such as camera or motion sensor cannot invent behavior. An authored fictional model is useful without claiming physical validation.

- [ ] Treat assembly replacement as an explicit execution boundary: retain the internal design, map the external interface, and stop the superseded evaluators. One active owner writes each governed output/state; multiple domains can coexist through declared exchanges. Physical connections can require a group solve or grouped model change. No solver/world per component, atom, pin or bone; no automatic duplicate power draw or parallel fine/coarse output writers.

- [ ] Allow imposed light, authored motion and other invented effects alongside physical models. Bind their influence on cameras, electrical detectors, contact or heat explicitly through supported adapters. A decorative light may illuminate a rendered image without entering a thermal balance. A physical study using imposed input retains that assumption in its results. Rendering, physical exchange, measurement and accepted operational facts remain distinct.

- [ ] Preserve the authored source when reducing work. Live transition declares carried/discarded state, mappings, initialization error, synchronization instant and continuation/restart behavior. A frozen state is not a cheaper evolving model; restored fine structure cannot recover untracked history. Source edits invalidate affected derived approximations unless an explicit retained approximation is selected with its limitations. Optional recording is not required to retain essential transition provenance.

- [ ] Scene defaults, assembly overrides and occurrence overrides resolve deterministically, with explicit domain/group constraints and an inspector showing the effective source of each setting. Automatic budget policy can choose only approved models that meet required outputs, validity and minimum accuracy; use measured cost, hysteresis and bounded switching overhead. A pinned scientific model is never silently downgraded. Offscreen causal dependencies remain active or follow an explicit approximation/pause policy. Viewer appearance choices never change shared authoritative behavior.

- [ ] Delivery follows named exports: durable model → frames/selections → shared local assets and editing. Functional devices, geography, CAD, character and molecule branches consume their actual subsets. Electronic structure branches into schematic/PCB realization and numerical circuit prerequisites; explicit joins prove the composed device. Each later science uses the same model/job/state contracts and its own actual inputs, without a blanket prior-stage sequence.

- [ ] Retain these cross-stage proofs: **B42** mixed lamp/sensor/camera/kinematic device, **B43** schematic/PCB/3D design, **B44** circuit-to-functional substitution. Their canonical specifications are owned by 07, 11a and 15a respectively. Later stages extend them without redefining their earlier acceptance. Freeze actual measured workload/error/resource limits before implementing each slice; plan edits do not retroactively change Stage 01 evidence.

## Numerical scope and independent scientific readiness

- [ ] Numerical and specialist Records remain unbuilt and require their own scoped implementation authorization. They may start after the graph's actual shared/domain prerequisites are verified; full-core acceptance is not a universal implementation dependency. The graph preserves the intended useful core and its final product acceptance rather than requiring every numerical field to be completed before a core release.
- [ ] Core use remains independent of numerical kernels: ordinary authored/functional devices, geometry/CAD/PCB checks, Walk/support, structural molecules and operational scenarios do not activate new physical solvers. A supply-available signal is not an electrical network, motion cooling is not temperature, and a molecular structure is not a validated force field.
- [ ] Retain all material, microscopic, rigid/joint, flexible/continuum, thermal, recording and specialist requirements with their owning branches. Domain-specific state transfer, physical coupling and calibration/validity are never supplied merely by the generic model envelope.
- [ ] Read-only results can be shared without their full private inputs/evaluator. Importing a definition does not execute code or allocate every alternative model. Numerical samples, replicas, output, peaks and continuing costs are independently admitted and metered.

